---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="What Counts as Debt? | ShouldISpend">
  <main style="max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 24px;">
    <p style="color:#0f766e; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:2px; font-weight:800;">
      Financial Basics
    </p>

    <h1 style="font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem); line-height: .95;">
      What Counts as Debt?
    </h1>

    <p>
      For ShouldISpend calculators, debt usually means recurring obligations or balances that reduce your financial flexibility.
    </p>

    <h2>Common examples of debt</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Credit card balances</li>
      <li>Student loans</li>
      <li>Auto loans</li>
      <li>Personal loans</li>
      <li>Medical debt</li>
      <li>Buy now, pay later balances</li>
      <li>Minimum monthly payments on borrowed money</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What about a mortgage?</h2>

    <p>
      A mortgage can count as debt, but for some calculators it may make more sense to separate housing costs from other debt payments.
    </p>

    <h2>Should I enter the full balance or monthly payment?</h2>

    <p>
      Use the label on each calculator. If it asks for monthly debt payments, enter the monthly amount. If it asks for total debt, enter the total balance.
    </p>

    <p>
      These tools are educational estimates, not financial advice. The goal is to make spending decisions clearer before you commit.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>